# Machine-local files and credentials
.DS_Store
._*
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# A local helper that waits for the LFS payloads and then starts the server. Anchored, because it
# lives at the repo root and a bare name would also swallow a same-named file in a subdirectory. It
# is not portable rather than merely personal: it hardcodes an absolute home path and checks for
# pointer stubs with `stat -f%z`, which is BSD-only and prints the filesystem type on Linux, so
# every good file would report as a stub there.
/run_when_ready.sh

# Harness settings hold a live ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN in plaintext. The whole directory is ignored
# rather than just that file, so a settings.local.json or a new credential file cannot slip in
# through `git add -A`.
.claude/

# Dependencies and caches
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.cache/
*.log
*.pid
*.blend1
*.blend2

# Local rollback archives and generated diagnostic captures
/backup/
/output/
/evidence/

# Browser-harness scratch: snapshots, traces and screenshots land in the working directory
.playwright-cli/
qm-*.png

# Runtime assets and authoritative production inputs are intentionally tracked.

# Reproducible web deployment output
/dist/
/.vercel/
.vercel
.env*

# Machine-local notes, one of which carries a login in plain text. Never commit.
remote_server.md

# Competition entries. They are filed elsewhere and are not part of the code, and the repository is
# public - so they are ignored rather than merely left untracked, which is what stops the next
# `git add -A` from picking them up.
/参赛*.md
/答辩*.html
